     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (850 mg three times daily with meals). It is well above the labeled limit even with normal kidney and liver function. At this dose the risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis, is high.\n\nCould you check what was intended? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day), which is the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin.\n- **1,700 mg per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily, which may be the source of the \"1700.\"\n- **A different dose or frequency**, such as 500 mg twice daily or 1,000 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
